ast in the fourth; and overall is a gold inescutcheon (a small shield placed in the centre of the large shield) charged with the red left hand of Ulster.", "reference": "1956 July, Col. H. C. B. Rogers, “Railway Heraldry”, in Railway Magazine, pages 476-477:"}, {"text": "This train is formed only of \"Blue Spot\" wagons for London; vans for Mac Fisheries Finsbury Park depot are marshalled at the rear to be detached at Finsbury Park.", "reference": "1963 December, “The fish traffic of Aberdeen”, in Modern Railways, page 389:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "подреждам"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "jäsentää"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "porządkować"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "uporządkować"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "organizar"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "выстра́ивать"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "упоря́дочивать"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "recopilar"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To ceremoniously guide, conduct or usher.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Our conquering ſwords ſhal marſhal vs the way\nUUe vſe to martch vpon the ſlaughtered foe:\nTrampling their bowels with our horſes hoofes: […]", "reference": "c. 1587–1588 (date written), [Christopher Marlowe], Tamburlaine the Great. […] The First Part […], 2nd edition, part 1, London: […] [R. Robinson for] Richard Iones, […], published 1592, →OCLC; reprinted as Tamburlaine the Great (A Scolar Press Facsimile), Menston, Yorkshire; London: Scolar Press, 1973, →ISBN, Act III, scene iii:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "johdattaa"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "opastaa"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name